{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":17346948,"ns":0,"title":"A¹ homotopy theory","extract":"In algebraic geometry and algebraic topology, branches of mathematics, A1 homotopy theory or motivic homotopy theory is a way to apply the techniques of algebraic topology, specifically homotopy, to algebraic varieties and, more generally, to schemes.  The theory is due to Fabien Morel and Vladimir Voevodsky.","description":"Application of homotopy to algebraic varieties","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}